# Applies the source edits that examples/torch/rm/README.md describes, after copying
# the MLCommons inference_results_v3.1 DLRM reference code into
# examples/torch/rm/utils/.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/mlcommons/inference_results_v3.1
#           closed/Intel/code/dlrm-v2-99/pytorch-cpu-int8/python
# Pinned commit: 951b4a7686692d1a0d9b9067a36a7fc26d72ada5
#
# 1. multihot_criteo.py  - EmbeddingBag offsets need batchsize + 1 entries, otherwise
#                          the last sample in every batch is dropped.
# 1b. multihot_criteo.py - read the .npy header through the public
#                          read_array_header_{1,0}/{2,0} entry points. NumPy 2.0 made
#                          numpy.lib private internals unreachable, so the original
#                          np.lib.format._read_array_header call raises AttributeError.
# 2. model/dlrm_model.py - replace MergedEmbeddingBagCat.forward() with a plain
#                          EmbeddingBag loop. The original int8 branch calls
#                          torch.ops.torch_ipex.merged_emb_with_cat, which requires
#                          intel-extension-for-pytorch.
# 3. backend_pytorch_native.py + model/dlrm_model.py - drop the module-level
#                          intel-extension-for-pytorch imports. After edit 2 the only
#                          remaining consumer is ipex.optimize() on the --use-bf16 path,
#                          which this example never takes, so the import moves into that
#                          branch instead of forcing an Intel CPU library onto every run.
#
# Apply it after copying the upstream code, from this directory:
#     patch -p1 -d utils --forward < dlrm_third_party.patch
